[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=GaloisField#doc\">docs#GaloisField</a> is currently an exposed declaration. However, even in pen and paper mathematics I'm mostly used to thinking of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb F_q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.975em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">F</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">q</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> as some sort of \"opaque\" object, characterized entirely by being a field of cardinality <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">q</span></span></span></span>. Would it make sense to mark it as <code>no_expose</code>? What sort of API, if any, would we require in order to access it?</p>",
        "id": 578513202,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773186774
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To me \"SplittingField\" is opaque enough that I didn't care much...<br>\nI guess one way to make it truly opaque while still usable, is to create an equivalence to the splitting field (instead of eq)?</p>",
        "id": 578513716,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773187119
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=SplittingField#doc\">docs#SplittingField</a> is also exposed btw.</p>",
        "id": 578513780,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773187170
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In fact, most of the file consists of auxiliary declarations which should surely be made private.</p>",
        "id": 578513935,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773187222
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I guess one doesn't need to add the equivalence because it already exists<br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Polynomial.IsSplittingField.algEquiv#doc\">docs#Polynomial.IsSplittingField.algEquiv</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=instIsSplittingFieldZModGaloisFieldHSubPolynomialHPowNatX#doc\">docs#instIsSplittingFieldZModGaloisFieldHSubPolynomialHPowNatX</a></p>",
        "id": 578514432,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773187512
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For whatever reason marking the <code>Field</code> instance for <code>SplittingField</code> as <code>no_expose</code> makes the <code>Algebra K (SplittingField f)</code> instance not be found... is this expected behavior?</p>",
        "id": 578518543,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773190486
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is this one of the <code>backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</code> problem?</p>",
        "id": 578519198,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773190953
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have no idea. Setting that option to false didn't seem to fix it.</p>",
        "id": 578519215,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773190970
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Then probably not</p>",
        "id": 578519296,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773190990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I <code>no_expose</code>d <code>GaloisField</code> and <code>SplittingField</code> in the draft PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37474\">#37474</a>.<br>\nIn spite of my efforts, it only improved one file.</p>\n<p>In my opinion, Lean does not have a rich enough ecosystem to <code>no_expose</code> types and instances.</p>",
        "id": 583169236,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1775096228
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>P.S. This performance improvement was offset by the new code to <code>no_expose</code> them.</p>",
        "id": 583169388,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1775096336
    }
]